237
00:20:13,576 --> 00:20:16,059
[SPEAKER_01]: Seems, like, more unpleasant initially.

238
00:20:16,975 --> 00:20:18,235
[SPEAKER_01]: But, eh... it's not.

239
00:20:18,975 --> 00:20:32,758
[SPEAKER_01]: If you... if you take that as a standard, you realize all these other things, all these other burdens of virtue and duty, that you have taken upon yourself as practice, will stop burdening you, because they will not be your duty anymore.

240
00:20:32,838 --> 00:20:35,819
[SPEAKER_01]: Your duty is to not act out of greed, aversion, delusion.

241
00:20:37,379 --> 00:20:41,720
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your duty is to not give in to a conscious choice,

242
00:20:43,297 --> 00:20:46,179
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do this because I'm pressured by the desire.

243
00:20:46,319 --> 00:20:48,721
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do this because I'm pressured by ill-will.

244
00:20:48,741 --> 00:20:51,783
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll do this because I'm indolent and I want to distract myself.

245
00:20:51,963 --> 00:20:52,323
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

246
00:20:52,363 --> 00:20:55,805
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all you need to do from the moment you wake up to the moment you go to sleep.

247
00:20:56,266 --> 00:20:58,707
[SPEAKER_01]: If you do that, you will be unable to break the precepts.

248
00:20:59,388 --> 00:21:05,852
[SPEAKER_01]: You will be unable to be discontented and you will be unable to not be composed.

249
00:21:07,693 --> 00:21:11,175
[SPEAKER_00]: Not being unable to not be practicing in line with

250
00:21:11,524 --> 00:21:11,924
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

251
00:21:12,685 --> 00:21:20,312
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, even if you don't think, oh, now I should practice in line with the dhamma, you will be practicing in line with the dhamma.

252
00:21:21,882 --> 00:21:26,484
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why I said, oh, how do we know, Master Gautama, what is in line with the dhamma, what it isn't?

253
00:21:26,544 --> 00:21:29,886
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, whatever brings dispassion, not passion.

254
00:21:30,466 --> 00:21:33,428
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever is inclined towards solitude, not company.

255
00:21:33,868 --> 00:21:36,149
[SPEAKER_01]: Towards disentanglement, not entanglement.

256
00:21:36,249 --> 00:21:41,532
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even if you don't necessarily want to give up the household life just yet, the principle remains the same.

257
00:21:42,818 --> 00:21:45,439
[SPEAKER_01]: You want to keep your mind free from disturbances and calm?

258
00:21:45,939 --> 00:21:50,761
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, keep an eye on the doorway of choice of acting out of greed, aversion, delusion.

259
00:21:51,241 --> 00:21:52,221
[SPEAKER_01]: And don't cover that up.

260
00:21:53,522 --> 00:21:54,642
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything else put aside.

261
00:21:54,722 --> 00:22:00,144
[SPEAKER_01]: Any sense of, oh, but I must do this, and I must do that, and I must practice ānāpānasati, and I must... No.

262
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:06,126
[SPEAKER_01]: You must develop the virtue that's unblemished, unbroken, until it becomes an aggregate on its own.

263
00:22:06,306 --> 00:22:07,267
[SPEAKER_01]: Something you're not doing.

264
00:22:08,092 --> 00:22:08,512
[SPEAKER_01]: anymore.

265
00:22:09,232 --> 00:22:14,213
[SPEAKER_01]: Something that's kind of there, because you've been abstaining from certain things long enough.

266
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:17,694
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, all you need to do is protect that virtue.

267
00:22:18,434 --> 00:22:19,995
[SPEAKER_01]: It will give you the context.

268
00:22:20,195 --> 00:22:21,915
[SPEAKER_01]: It will give you the samādhi on account of it.

269
00:22:21,955 --> 00:22:27,696
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, again, the doorway of where all the problems come in, is greed, aversion, delusion.

270
00:22:28,256 --> 00:22:30,897
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not lapse of mindfulness or not enough focusing.

271
00:22:32,117 --> 00:22:36,158
[SPEAKER_00]: You are training yourself to see that doorway clearer and clearer and clearer.

272
00:22:40,081 --> 00:22:40,742
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

273
00:22:41,182 --> 00:22:49,748
[SPEAKER_01]: And training to see where that doorway is, it's not on the level of training your focusing practice.

274
00:22:50,148 --> 00:22:52,710
[SPEAKER_01]: They will then reveal the glimpse of the doorway.

275
00:22:52,890 --> 00:22:54,171
[SPEAKER_01]: The doorway is not a glimpse.

276
00:22:54,331 --> 00:22:55,432
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a split second.

277
00:22:55,532 --> 00:22:59,335
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the entire context that basically directs your entire day.

278
00:22:59,875 --> 00:23:00,275
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

279
00:23:01,056 --> 00:23:06,600
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your entire day, actions throughout that day, choices you're making, are very conscious things.

280
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,101
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where the doorway is.

281
00:23:08,951 --> 00:23:11,433
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you don't need the focusing to see the doorway.

282
00:23:11,753 --> 00:23:13,414
[SPEAKER_01]: You need honesty to see it.

283
00:23:14,095 --> 00:23:17,958
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, initially, like, oh, okay, I will not engage with unwholesome.

284
00:23:18,298 --> 00:23:22,301
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, the stress and the pain of pressure will be there, will increase.

285
00:23:23,081 --> 00:23:25,783
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you realize, okay, what do I do now?

