00:23:56,636 --> 00:24:00,078
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's like, well, no, actually, you're not supposed to relieve yourself from it.

293
00:24:00,218 --> 00:24:06,142
[SPEAKER_01]: You're supposed to not break the precepts on account of it, and that's how you will calm down.

294
00:24:06,742 --> 00:24:08,743
[SPEAKER_00]: I was thinking, you know, you can... so you can...

295
00:24:09,158 --> 00:24:12,500
You do all this renunciation and this pressure is building up.

296
00:24:13,161 --> 00:24:14,421
It's unpleasant.

297
00:24:15,442 --> 00:24:21,786
And then you can realize that it's unpleasant because I'm doing it correctly.

298
00:24:22,186 --> 00:24:23,847
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah.

299
00:24:23,887 --> 00:24:24,628
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm cleaning it out.

300
00:24:24,668 --> 00:24:27,590
[SPEAKER_00]: So, oh yeah, I'm doing it correctly.

301
00:24:27,670 --> 00:24:27,910
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

302
00:24:29,071 --> 00:24:29,731
[SPEAKER_00]: Isn't that great?

303
00:24:29,991 --> 00:24:32,093
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's that other other other talks we mentioned.

304
00:24:32,133 --> 00:24:37,176
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, the pressure that's building up on account of your renunciation is not because of the renunciation.

305
00:24:38,122 --> 00:24:39,963
[SPEAKER_01]: It's because of that which you are renouncing.

306
00:24:43,026 --> 00:24:50,992
[SPEAKER_01]: So, your renunciation reveals, basically, what you were under, what was controlling you, reveals your addiction.

307
00:24:52,173 --> 00:24:54,575
[SPEAKER_01]: And abstaining from the addictive substance,

308
00:24:56,921 --> 00:25:08,709
[SPEAKER_01]: So it feels like there is no problem up until I started saying no to myself.

309
00:25:09,690 --> 00:25:15,834
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like saying no to yourself only has revealed what you were already victim of, so to speak.

