00:25:15,854 --> 00:25:24,700
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in order to develop that aggregate of virtue, correctly, eh... whether you are a layperson or a summoner,

311
00:25:26,235 --> 00:25:29,296
[SPEAKER_01]: You will also then see, like, the role of patience.

312
00:25:29,977 --> 00:25:31,497
[SPEAKER_01]: Why that patience is important.

313
00:25:32,198 --> 00:25:34,259
[SPEAKER_01]: Not, you know, not like, not in that sense, oh, be patient.

314
00:25:34,279 --> 00:25:35,979
[SPEAKER_01]: Patience is important and it's a virtue.

315
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:54,968
[SPEAKER_01]: No, it's like a, it's, it's, it's a, it's a thing you can do and develop and, you know, it's useful to remind yourself of it, because withdrawing from things that pressure you will, will, will reveal that, as I said, the, the pain of that pressure, it will increase it.

316
00:25:55,983 --> 00:26:05,750
[SPEAKER_01]: So, unless you have patience to bear it, you will then give in to that, eh... motivation and need and craving to get rid of it.

317
00:26:06,771 --> 00:26:13,235
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you might not break the precepts, but you still want to get rid of the discomfort that they revealed.

318
00:26:15,097 --> 00:26:16,018
[SPEAKER_01]: And how'd you do that?

319
00:26:16,098 --> 00:26:19,040
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you do that by following, eh...

320
00:26:19,652 --> 00:26:24,034
[SPEAKER_01]: Tradition, technique, practices in that impersonal manner.

321
00:26:24,154 --> 00:26:27,555
[SPEAKER_01]: And by that, I mean in that, like, oh, I just do that because that's what we are supposed to do.

322
00:26:28,155 --> 00:26:30,296
[SPEAKER_01]: I do that because that's what technique tells me to do.

323
00:26:31,017 --> 00:26:37,759
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you will find ways of doing things in that... in a way that would basically mask your responsibility for it.

324
00:26:37,779 --> 00:26:41,801
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's how you will alleviate the discomfort that a virtue placed upon you.

325
00:26:42,101 --> 00:26:44,002
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you must actually not do that.

326
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:52,118
[SPEAKER_01]: You mustn't give in to those ways of management, even if they seemingly are aligning themselves with the dhamma practice.

327
00:26:52,759 --> 00:26:56,659
[SPEAKER_01]: The point is, you are doing them because you want to manage the discomfort.

328
00:26:56,779 --> 00:26:57,880
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't want to endure it.

329
00:26:58,280 --> 00:27:02,020
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in other words, you are acting out of craving against the unpleasant feeling.

330
00:27:02,261 --> 00:27:06,061
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why you cannot be free from craving just yet, because you keep maintaining it.

331
00:27:07,142 --> 00:27:08,602
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why virtue in itself

332
00:27:09,625 --> 00:27:15,527
[SPEAKER_01]: Without a right view, without right instruction, will just be virtue, you know.

333
00:27:15,627 --> 00:27:21,229
[SPEAKER_01]: It will not necessarily give rise to understanding of the Four Noble Truths and the way out of suffering.

334
00:27:22,529 --> 00:27:38,094
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the discomfort that comes on account of virtue, sense restraint, self-control, is... that's... that discomfort mustn't be, eh... covered up, eh... dismissed, ignored,

335
00:27:39,088 --> 00:27:41,189
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, or, or, you know, got rid of.

336
00:27:42,670 --> 00:27:44,850
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that discomfort must be accepted.

337
00:27:45,851 --> 00:27:47,732
[SPEAKER_01]: You must be patient in regard to it.

338
00:27:48,792 --> 00:27:55,895
[SPEAKER_01]: You must actually look more at your attitude of gratuitously trying to get rid of the discomfort, then you should be looking at the discomfort.

339
00:27:56,695 --> 00:28:02,778
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, if you want to practice samādhi within that, well, you will realize, okay, samādhi within the discomfort.

340
00:28:03,409 --> 00:28:04,589
[SPEAKER_01]: Not at the expense of it.

341
00:28:04,649 --> 00:28:05,530
[SPEAKER_01]: Not instead of it.

342
00:28:06,050 --> 00:28:08,731
[SPEAKER_01]: So, samādhi doesn't mean disappearance of discomfort.

343
00:28:09,251 --> 00:28:13,252
[SPEAKER_01]: Samādhi means I am now unmoved by any discomfort.

344
00:28:14,833 --> 00:28:16,093
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's a very different thing.

345
00:28:16,674 --> 00:28:23,116
[SPEAKER_01]: Not necessarily externally looking by what you're doing, but internally it's rooted in a completely different intention.

346
00:28:23,716 --> 00:28:25,597
[SPEAKER_01]: One is wholesome, another one is unwholesome.

347
00:28:27,337 --> 00:28:28,598
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why that patience

348
00:28:29,535 --> 00:28:33,898
[SPEAKER_01]: It's necessary for you to endure the discomfort without habitually trying to get rid of it.

349
00:28:35,219 --> 00:28:39,022
[SPEAKER_01]: Because then, again, you're still acting on the level of that sense response.

350
00:28:39,242 --> 00:28:40,223
[SPEAKER_01]: Pleasing, give it to me.

351
00:28:40,263 --> 00:28:41,604
[SPEAKER_01]: Displeasing, get rid of it.

352
00:28:42,164 --> 00:28:46,107
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly what it means by, you know, even meditation is rooted in sensuality.

353
00:28:46,247 --> 00:28:47,428
[SPEAKER_01]: It's still the same principle.

354
00:28:48,925 --> 00:28:56,909
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you're patient with it, able to endure it sufficiently enough, you will learn how to calm yourself within it, not the expense of it.

355
00:28:57,609 --> 00:29:01,971
[SPEAKER_01]: And, of course, you will see what the true problem is, which wasn't the discomfort.

356
00:29:02,031 --> 00:29:03,232
[SPEAKER_01]: That was not the root of suffering.

357
00:29:03,492 --> 00:29:07,354
[SPEAKER_01]: Your craving against it was the root of suffering.

358
00:29:07,514 --> 00:29:10,155
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, all you need to do is recollect the virtue.

359
00:29:11,598 --> 00:29:21,626
[SPEAKER_01]: On account of which, you're already patient and contented, and you will already be calm, regardless of whether it's comfort or discomfort around you, because you know exactly what not to do.

360
00:29:23,948 --> 00:29:32,355
[SPEAKER_01]: And you don't need to worry about, then, what should I do, because you're not trying to get rid of the pain gratuitously anymore.

361
00:29:34,717 --> 00:29:36,938
Just refining, refining, refining your breath.

362
00:29:37,019 --> 00:29:37,119
Hm.

363
00:29:37,979 --> 00:29:39,921
Are the same principles from the start?

364
00:29:40,181 --> 00:29:40,481
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

365
00:29:41,678 --> 00:29:45,100
[SPEAKER_00]: Engaging with anything unwholesome and craving is unwholesome.

366
00:29:45,880 --> 00:29:46,060
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

367
00:29:47,441 --> 00:29:54,545
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if the pain feels like, oh, the pain is too much, I don't know what to do, well, fine, but you know exactly what not to do.

368
00:29:56,246 --> 00:30:00,548
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't break the precepts, don't compromise the virtue, do everything else within that.

369
00:30:02,749 --> 00:30:09,053
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't neglect sense restraint and so on, which means, okay, so, I don't need to do anything, as long as I don't do things I know I shouldn't be doing.

370
00:30:09,633 --> 00:30:09,953
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

371
00:30:12,770 --> 00:30:18,154
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how you actually calm yourself within that which is pressuring you and which you're enduring.

372
00:30:18,174 --> 00:30:21,277
[SPEAKER_01]: Because people are always pressured internally by that.

373
00:30:22,058 --> 00:30:22,858
[SPEAKER_01]: What do I do?

374
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:24,179
[SPEAKER_01]: How do I react?

375
00:30:24,660 --> 00:30:28,443
[SPEAKER_01]: What, you know, what is my next move in order to deal with this?

376
00:30:28,603 --> 00:30:32,586
[SPEAKER_01]: Which all carries that view, that kind of, this must be dealt with.

377
00:30:32,666 --> 00:30:33,927
[SPEAKER_01]: And you're burdened by that.

378
00:30:34,067 --> 00:30:35,108
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the pain of it.

379
00:30:36,849 --> 00:30:38,631
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you realize, actually, I don't need to do anything.

380
00:30:39,432 --> 00:30:41,093
[SPEAKER_01]: I know what I'm not going to do.

381
00:30:41,293 --> 00:30:47,598
[SPEAKER_01]: I know what I'm... what I shouldn't be doing, but that requires no effort now, because I've been following that lifestyle for a while.

382
00:30:48,678 --> 00:30:52,561
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you're not burdened by any response or any... any sort of figuring it out.

383
00:30:52,641 --> 00:30:53,421
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't really matter.

384
00:30:53,702 --> 00:30:56,564
[SPEAKER_01]: All that matters is to not do what you know you're not supposed to do.

385
00:30:57,204 --> 00:30:58,445
[SPEAKER_01]: Act out of great aversion and delusion.

386
00:31:02,588 --> 00:31:03,728
It's a hard thing to do.

387
00:31:04,409 --> 00:31:04,609
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

388
00:31:06,050 --> 00:31:06,490
[SPEAKER_01]: Initially.

389
00:31:07,071 --> 00:31:08,912
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, the more you do it, the easier it becomes.

